# Commit identity

The `identity` job in `.github/workflows/tests.yml` runs `harness/check_commit_identity.py`.
It fails any commit not on `main` whose author email, committer email, or trailer email is
not exactly `73196388+njs14@users.noreply.github.com`.

Before the first commit in a session, run:

```sh
git config user.name njs14
git config user.email 73196388+njs14@users.noreply.github.com
```

Before every push:

1. Rewrite any commit authored or committed as Cursor Agent (`cursoragent@cursor.com`) to the
   identity above, for example with
   `git rebase origin/main --exec 'git commit --amend --no-edit --reset-author'`.
2. Drop `Co-authored-by` trailers. If a trailer must stay, it uses
   `73196388+njs14@users.noreply.github.com`, never `njs14@users.noreply.github.com`.
3. Run `CHECK_HEAD=HEAD python3 harness/check_commit_identity.py` and push only when it prints
   `commit identity ok`.
